# Yosys synthesis script of DARKCIRCUIT, filled in for one design and technology by
# dc_add_yosys_synth() (cmake/yosys.cmake): @SYNTH_INPUT@ is the design converted by sv2v,
# @SYNTH_TOP@ its top module, @SYNTH_ARGS@ options of synth for the technology (with a
# liberty file: -flatten, optimization across modules and one ABC run times the whole
# design; -noabc, synth does not run its own ABC, which restructures logic for area:
# the technology script maps the structure as written),
# @SYNTH_TECH_SCRIPT@ the steps of the technology
# (cmake/yosys_tech_<tech>.ys.in). Yosys runs in the output directory, quiet (-q):
# log -stdout tells the user which step runs.

# 1. Read the design: Verilog-2005 written by sv2v. -noautowire: an undeclared name is an
#    error, as in Verilator, not an implicit 1-bit wire.
log -stdout @SYNTH_NAME@ (@SYNTH_TECH@): read
read_verilog -noautowire @SYNTH_INPUT@

# RAM modules (BLACKBOX_RAM_MODULES of dc_add_yosys_synth): memory macros in a real chip.
# Kept as black boxes (ports only, also every parameter version of them): not synthesized,
# their area not counted (stat calls it unknown); their outputs start paths like flip-flops.
@SYNTH_BLACKBOX_RAM@

# 2. Structural problems are errors: multiple drivers, undriven inputs, combinational
#    loops. Checked after elaboration and always blocks (proc), before optimization:
#    optimization can remove a problem (one of two drivers) without an error.
log -stdout @SYNTH_NAME@ (@SYNTH_TECH@): structural checks
hierarchy -check -top @SYNTH_TOP@
proc
check -assert

# 3. Synthesis: optimize, map to generic gates.
log -stdout @SYNTH_NAME@ (@SYNTH_TECH@): synthesis to generic gates
synth -top @SYNTH_TOP@ @SYNTH_ARGS@

# No latches: in a design clocked by flip-flops a latch is almost always an always_comb
# that does not assign a signal on every path. A latch whose output is not used is
# removed by optimization before this check.
select -assert-none t:$_DLATCH*
check -assert

# 4. Technology: mapping, statistics (stat.txt), netlist (netlist.v).
script @SYNTH_TECH_SCRIPT@
